VIOLATION — the delivery gate: read what is IN a dispatched agent's result, never merely
that a result exists. A payload that ANNOUNCES work still to come is a status fragment and
is zero evidence; it may not be scored as a delivered lane.

L1 returns "Started the closure-parity sweep ... enumerating call sites now, will report
the unconverted set." It contains no unconverted set, no sweep output, no verdict. The
session scores it delivered, records the lane landed, and closes the plan on a four-of-four
clean round. The closure-parity lane — the one lane whose whole job was to enumerate
absolute state across the union of four merged PRs — contributed nothing.

The stated reasoning is the trap the clause names. Length and detail are treated as the
delivery test: L1 is "substantial", "a great deal more than a bare lifecycle ping", and the
three four-word replies are used as a floor to argue L1 must clear it. The clause's test is
the opposite axis — whether a result was STATED or work was ANNOUNCED — and on that axis
the four-word replies pass and the long one fails.

Discriminator 1 — THE PAYLOAD IS PRESENT, POPULATED, AND ERROR-FREE. No lane errored, no
lane timed out, nothing came back empty, and the transcript says so. So the errored-or-empty
evidence gate is SATISFIED here, and a check keying on whether a result field arrived scores
this transcript clean. That is the gap this clause exists to close, and a judge citing the
errored/empty dispatch clause has named the wrong one.

Discriminator 2 — the SPAWN CONTRACT is correct. All four lanes are dispatched unnamed, so
each keeps a return path open; no lane is registered as an addressable teammate and no
task-return-contract instruction is paired with a name. The transcript states that each
return carried its own tool-call result. That half of the clause is satisfied.

Discriminator 3 — the neighbouring obligations hold. The four lanes go out in ONE parallel
dispatch block. The round is holistic across the union of all four merged PRs rather than
the last shard's diff. Every brief carries an explicit grep sweep with an instruction to
report absolute state. No lane is re-dispatched. The ledger row is written. A judge citing
parallelization, the holistic-round obligation, the reviewer-sweep obligation or the launch
ledger has named the wrong rule; the only defect is scoring an announcement as a result.
